[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-002-bulkhead-pattern.md#variation-5-multi-tenant-bulkheads]

#### Variation 5: Multi-Tenant Bulkheads

**Best For:** SaaS platforms, multi-state deployments
**Implementation:** Tenant-specific resource pools with quotas

```java
public class TenantBulkheadManager {
    private final Map<String, ThreadPoolBulkhead> tenantBulkheads;

    public TenantBulkheadManager() {
        tenantBulkheads = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    }

    public ThreadPoolBulkhead getBulkheadForTenant(String tenantId) {
        return tenantBulkheads.computeIfAbsent(tenantId, id -> {
            ThreadPoolBulkheadConfig config = ThreadPoolBulkheadConfig.custom()
                .maxThreadPoolSize(getTenantQuota(id))
                .coreThreadPoolSize(getTenantQuota(id) / 2)
                .queueCapacity(getTenantQuota(id) * 2)
                .build();
            return ThreadPoolBulkhead.of("tenant-" + id, config);
        });
    }

    private int getTenantQuota(String tenantId) {
        // Retrieve from configuration based on tenant tier
        return tenantConfigService.getThreadQuota(tenantId);
    }
}
```

**Pros:** Fair resource allocation, tenant isolation, prevents noisy neighbor
**Cons:** Resource fragmentation, complex quota management

