### Real-World Example 1: Claims Processing Service with EDI Gateway Isolation

**Context:**
The Claims Processing service handles 500K+ daily claims for multiple state Medicaid programs. The service integrates with an external EDI clearinghouse for electronic claim submission, which historically experiences periodic latency spikes (from 500ms baseline to 25+ seconds). Prior to bulkhead implementation, EDI latency issues caused complete service outages affecting all claim operations.

**Problem Scenario (Pre-Bulkhead):**
```text
March 2024 Incident:
Time: 10:15 AM EST

- EDI clearinghouse latency spike: 500ms → 28 seconds
- Claims service shared thread pool (200 threads) exhausted
- All operations blocked (claim adjudication, status lookup, document retrieval)
- Provider portal completely unavailable
- 47-minute outage
- Impact: 12,400 claims delayed, SLA penalty incurred
```

**Implementation:**

1. **Bulkhead Design:**
```java
// BulkheadConfiguration.java
@Configuration
public class ClaimsBulkheadConfiguration {

    @Bean
    public ThreadPoolBulkhead claimAdjudicationBulkhead() {
        return ThreadPoolBulkhead.of("claimAdjudication",
            ThreadPoolBulkheadConfig.custom()
                .maxThreadPoolSize(80)        // Critical: 40% of total
                .coreThreadPoolSize(40)
                .queueCapacity(200)
                .build());
    }

    @Bean
    public ThreadPoolBulkhead ediSubmissionBulkhead() {
        return ThreadPoolBulkhead.of("ediSubmission",
            ThreadPoolBulkheadConfig.custom()
                .maxThreadPoolSize(40)        // Standard: 20% of total
                .coreThreadPoolSize(20)
                .queueCapacity(50)
                .build());
    }

    @Bean
    public ThreadPoolBulkhead statusLookupBulkhead() {
        return ThreadPoolBulkhead.of("statusLookup",
            ThreadPoolBulkheadConfig.custom()
                .maxThreadPoolSize(50)        // Standard: 25% of total
                .coreThreadPoolSize(25)
                .queueCapacity(100)
                .build());
    }

    @Bean
    public SemaphoreBulkhead documentRetrievalBulkhead() {
        return SemaphoreBulkhead.of("documentRetrieval",
            SemaphoreBulkheadConfig.custom()
                .maxConcurrentCalls(30)       // Remaining capacity
                .maxWaitDuration(Duration.ofMillis(500))
                .build());
    }
}
```

2. **Service Implementation:**
```java
@Service
public class ClaimsService {

    @Autowired private ThreadPoolBulkhead claimAdjudicationBulkhead;
    @Autowired private ThreadPoolBulkhead ediSubmissionBulkhead;
    @Autowired private CircuitBreaker ediCircuitBreaker;

    public CompletableFuture<ClaimResult> adjudicateClaim(Claim claim) {
        return claimAdjudicationBulkhead.executeSupplier(() -> {
            log.info("Adjudicating claim {} in isolated bulkhead", claim.getId());

            // Core adjudication logic (database intensive)
            ClaimResult result = adjudicationEngine.process(claim);

            // Persist result
            claimRepository.save(result);

            return result;
        });
    }

    public CompletableFuture<EdiResponse> submitToEDI(ClaimResult result) {
        // Combine bulkhead + circuit breaker for EDI calls
        Supplier<EdiResponse> supplier = () -> ediClient.submit(result);

        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
            Decorators.ofSupplier(supplier)
                .withThreadPoolBulkhead(ediSubmissionBulkhead)
                .withCircuitBreaker(ediCircuitBreaker)
                .withFallback(
                    Arrays.asList(BulkheadFullException.class, CallNotPermittedException.class),
                    ex -> {
                        log.warn("EDI submission bulkhead exhausted, queuing for retry");
                        retryQueue.enqueue(result);
                        return EdiResponse.queued();
                    })
                .decorate()
        );
    }
}
```

